course: dictionary
lesson: 5274
title: Names that become words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter often shows a name, a special person or place. Judas is a name: «Judas, one of the twelve disciples, betrayed Jesus to the authorities for thirty pieces of silver.» Here the clue is the capital J and the words «one of the twelve disciples», which tell you Judas is a person.
explain: Some names turn into everyday words. A «Judas» (small j, no capital) can mean a traitor, someone who betrays a friend. The word «betrayed» is your clue: to betray someone is to turn against a person who trusts you. So a Judas is a person who does this.
explain: Calling someone a Judas is a strong insult, so use it carefully. A «Judas kiss» is a show of friendship that hides betrayal: the kiss looks friendly, but the friend is secretly turning against you. Always check the clues before you decide what a word means.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a word often shows a name, such as Judas.
fact: «Judas» (name) means Judas Iscariot, one of Jesus' twelve disciples, who betrayed him for thirty pieces of silver.
fact: «A Judas» (noun) means someone who betrays a friend; it is a strong insult.
fact: «Betray» means to give away or turn against someone who trusts you.
fact: Another disciple, Jude, had almost the same name but was faithful, so check which Judas is meant.
exercise: «Judas, one of the twelve disciples, betrayed Jesus to the authorities for thirty pieces of silver.» What does betrayed mean here? | Gave a present to | Ran away from a race | Sang a song for | *Turned against and gave away someone who trusted him
exercise: Ella's friend told everyone her secret. Ella shouts, «You Judas!» What does she mean? | *You betrayed my trust, like someone who gives away a friend | You are a brilliant dancer | You are my cousin
exercise: In «Judas, one of the twelve disciples, betrayed Jesus», what tells you Judas is a name? | It rhymes with Jesus | It comes after the word one | *It has a capital letter and it names a person | It is a colour
test: «He gave away his friend's secret, so Sam called him a Judas.» What does a Judas mean here? | A very fast runner | A quiet, shy boy | *Someone who betrays a friend | A kind helper
test: Jude was another disciple with almost the same name as Judas. What does faithful mean? | Loud | *Loyal and true, never betraying a friend | Forgetful | Lazy
exam: «Judas kept the disciples' money bag and used to help himself to what was put into it.» What does «help himself» suggest about Judas? | Generous, giving it away | Lost in the garden | Happy and kind | *Greedy, taking what was not his
